9
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:34,920
Could you grab them for me, please?

10
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:48,840
P'Three, why aren't you
wearing any clothes?

11
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:52,360
Why are you coming in?

12
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:53,920
I'm just bringing you your clothes.

13
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:55,640
What kind of dirty thoughts
are you having?

14
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:59,600
Shouldn't you go
put some clothes on first?

15
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:01,600
I'm gonna do some laundry.

16
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:04,840
Or do you think...

17
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:08,280
I'm going to do something to you?

18
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:15,800
And don't keep me waiting.

19
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:19,640
I'm showering after you.

20
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:21,960
Okay.

21
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:30,320
Hey.

22
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:33,320
What? Are you scared
I'll see your willy?

23
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:35,320
Please get out. I'm going to shower.

24
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:39,440
We've both got it. Why be embarrassed?

25
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:44,240
Maybe what's different
is the confidence level.

26
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:46,600
Whoa, hey, what are you trying to say?

27
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:48,920
- You're confident? Let me see.
- P'Three, get out!

28
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,520
- Are you really that confident?
- This isn't meant for...

29
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:51,600
- Get out!
- What?

30
00:01:57,160 --> 00:02:01,840
♪Birthday but with me♪

31
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:05,240
♪Every time, it's just me and me only♪

32
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:08,880
♪What's this feeling? I've got no clue,♪

33
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,960
♪Could it be I'm missing you?♪

34
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:12,360
♪(Am I missing you?)♪

35
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:17,160
♪Birthday but with me♪

36
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:20,240
♪Why is it always happening to me?♪

37
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:24,000
♪The more it happens, the more I see♪

38
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:26,880
♪Yeah, it must be♪

39
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:53,200
P'Three's up early.

40
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:03,120
Yeah, move.

41
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:04,560
Finish them off.

42
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:07,520
Not bad at all.

43
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:09,080
- Sh*t!
- Oh...

44
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:10,560
You startled me.

45
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,080
I'm the one who's startled.

46
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,320
When did you get here?

47
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:18,600
Just a moment
before you started the match.

48
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:23,440
Did you wake up early,
or have you been up all night?

49
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:33,000
My biological clock
always wakes me up around this time.

50
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:35,560
My body is craving caffeine.

51
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:36,920
Morning coffee, you know?

52
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:40,160
Did you actually get some sleep?

53
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,240
How am I supposed to sleep?

54
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:00,560
Soh...

55
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:07,120
Seriously?

56
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,640
I'm gonna embarrass you
when you wake up.

57
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:56,480
I'll just go sleep
in the living room, then.

58
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:07,720
Or...

59
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:18,640
Was I moving around so much in my sleep

60
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:21,280
that you couldn't get any rest?

61
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:22,920
- I'm sorry.
- Hey, no. No.

62
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:23,840
It's just...

63
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:26,520
my body's full of energy,

64
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:30,040
so I had to get up early
and get some practice in.

65
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:31,960
Practice over, energy spent.

66
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:34,000
Better top up with some coffee.

67
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,800
Whoa, are you drinking two cups?

68
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,400
Your heart might race.

69
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:42,920
Just a little coffee

70
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:45,640
won't affect my heart
as much as being near you.

71
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:48,960
Oh...

72
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:53,960
So, sleeping next to me last night...

73
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:56,440
made your heart race so much
that you couldn't sleep,

74
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:58,400
right?

75
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:05,400
Man, you're getting good
at these cheesy jokes, aren't you?

76
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:07,080
Go.

77
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:08,600
Go shower and brush your teeth.

78
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:09,720
I already squeezed
the toothpaste out for you.

79
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:11,520
And I'll take you to your condo.

80
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:12,960
Roger that.

81
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:24,720
Soh, I'll see you again this evening.

82
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:26,320
I'm taking you to the training camp.

83
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,200
Training camp?

84
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:29,280
Yeah.

85
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:42,920
Hello, everyone.

86
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:45,480
Today, welcome to "Blue Viper Time."

87
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:47,560
It's me, Peem.

88
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:51,320
Guys, the Pro League
is just around the corner,

89
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:54,040
so I'd like to show you
our training camp

90
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:56,080
to see what the vibe is like here.

91
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:58,480
In this first zone,
they're working really hard.

92
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:00,800
It's a place
for all our players to practice.

93
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:03,280
You're practicing
quite intensely, right, Meen?

94
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:05,600
- Yes, we are.
- Am I interrupting?

95
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:06,200
No.

96
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:07,040
Oh, okay.

97
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:08,320
How's it going? Busy practicing?

98
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:10,920
- Yeah. We have to...
- You're checking the enemy's strategy?

99
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:14,240
Whoa. Alright,
I'd better not disturb her.

100
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:15,040
She's super focused.

101
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:17,400
Anyway, let's see what ALONEW is doing.

102
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:19,080
- Hello.
- How are things, our MVP?

103
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:21,800
- Practicing with a new hero.
- A new hero? Wow.

104
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:23,000
Oops, am I spoiling the plan?

105
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:24,800
Will this be released
before or after the match?

106
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:26,040
I'd better not bother him.

107
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:29,000
Let him focus
on the new hero he's practicing with.

108
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:31,040
The next zone is for the coach.

109
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:33,200
I have to keep my voice down,
or the coach will scold me.

110
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:36,800
He analyzes the strategies
for both our team...

111
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:37,880
and the opposing team.

112
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:41,960
He gives excellent advice
to the Blue Viper players.

113
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:45,320
That's why Blue Viper
is a title contender every year.

114
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:47,960
It's only to be expected,
especially with me around.

115
00:07:48,840 --> 00:07:51,160
Alright, let's move on to the next zone.

116
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:53,120
This is the chill zone

117
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:57,080
where we have various games to play
besides the one we compete in.

118
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,800
- And there's a sitting area...
- Wait,

119
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:00,360
does a training camp
have to be this fancy?

120
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:01,280
Of course.

121
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:03,160
This is Blue Viper's camp, man.

122
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:05,080
They're the undefeated kings
of the Pro League

123
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,280
who have won almost every year.

124
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:08,520
They've got tens of millions
invested in the team.

125
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:11,840
I bet these players
are making six figures.

126
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:14,800
I knew gaming could make you money,

127
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:16,560
but I didn't think
it would be this much.

128
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:19,320
Man, the Pro League is no joke.

129
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:21,920
It's where the country's top players
face off against each other.

130
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:24,800
And you're about to be one of them.

131
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:27,360
Holy sh*t!

132
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:30,600
Our friend is going to be
a full-time esports athlete soon.

133
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,440
That's so cool.

134
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:35,080
With good food
and a nice place like this,

135
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:36,360
I could practice all day long.

136
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:37,360
Me, too.

137
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:41,840
Welcome to the B.S. Brothers' camp!

138
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:53,800
There it is.

139
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:57,480
Oh, for God's sake.

140
00:08:58,080 --> 00:09:01,200
You made such a grand entrance,

141
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:05,600
but this place is a total sh*thole.

142
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:09,400
Hey, make yourselves at home.

143
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:11,560
Just think of this as your second home.

144
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:13,160
Okay.

145
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,760
Let me give you a tour.

146
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:20,680
This room right here
is what we call "The Base."

147
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:22,640
It's a very important room

148
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:24,800
because all our strategies and plans

149
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:27,320
can never leak out from here.

150
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:28,920
They must stay within these walls.

151
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:33,560
Why do you have to be so dramatic?

152
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:35,560
Just call it what it is,
the training room.

153
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:42,960
Now, if you want to relax,

154
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,400
there's an internet cafe downstairs.

155
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:46,800
After gaming, you might get tired

156
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:48,840
and feel like you're dying, right?

157
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:49,840
Just head next door.

158
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:51,800
The massage lady there
has hands of gold.

159
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,440
Our team gets three meals a day.

160
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:56,600
The food's cooked by P'Jane.

161
00:09:56,760 --> 00:09:58,600
Trust me, it's damn delicious.

162
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:00,280
If you don't believe me, here's proof.

163
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:01,680
Just check out P'Toobtub's body.

164
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:03,080
That's all the proof you need.

165
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:05,320
If you're worried
about gaining weight, don't be

166
00:10:05,360 --> 00:10:06,200
because we have...

167
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:08,160
a mini-gym.

168
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:13,720
Okay.

169
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:22,680
Anyway, that's enough
for the introductions.

170
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:24,480
Alright? Let's go practice.

171
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:25,960
- Let's go, baby. Let's go.
- Hold on!

172
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:29,440
Hey, newbie.

173
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,240
Since you stepped into this room,

174
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:33,480
have you greeted the owner yet?

175
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:35,680
The owner?

176
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:38,440
- Who is it?
- Jeez.

177
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:40,120
- He's right here.
- Right here.

178
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:44,800
This used to be
P'Toobtub's grandma's room.

179
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:47,280
She was bedridden for years.

180
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:49,560
After she passed away in that bed,

181
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:53,240
we turned it into this training camp.

182
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:55,400
But I've heard some things.

183
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:57,400
Your team's situation
isn't looking too good.

184
00:10:58,160 --> 00:10:59,600
You guys are at the bottom
of the league,

185
00:11:00,080 --> 00:11:01,560
and your teammates play like trash.

186
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:03,400
They end up in last place every year.

187
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:05,560
It's a total disaster waiting to happen.

188
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:08,320
Honestly, they're definitely
using you to carry them.

189
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,080
You're in for a rough time, buddy.

190
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:13,320
Anyway, just think of it as your debut.

191
00:11:13,880 --> 00:11:15,960
Maybe another team
will scout you and sign you.

192
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:17,240
Right?

193
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:31,160
(One month before the Pro League)

194
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:32,560
We've got everything here.

195
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:34,400
The whole team's here, you know?

196
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:41,960
- P'Laem, don't be scared. Dive in!
- Yeah!

197
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,920
- Here. Right here.
- I know, I know!

198
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:44,880
- No, right here.
- Jeez!

199
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:47,480
Dammit! If you don't stop,
I'm gonna kick both your asses.

200
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:49,200
You're both getting it now.
Get over here!

201
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:52,000
- P'Soh!
- Hey...

202
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,160
Help me, P'Soh!

203
00:11:57,880 --> 00:11:59,640
Hey, watch it, Derpy Kid!

204
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:02,960
(First Blood)

205
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,760
Good thing I tanked that damage in time.

206
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:08,440
- Guys!
- Come on!

207
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:10,000
Time for Laem's solo!

208
00:12:16,800 --> 00:12:17,840
Go ahead, let it all out.

209
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:30,800
A defensive item with full coverage.

210
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:44,960
Hey, Soh, fall back. You're gonna die.

211
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:57,760
Man, we're toast.

212
00:12:58,400 --> 00:13:00,520
Losing nonstop like this
is just too much.

213
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:03,600
I think we should go with Plan M.

214
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:05,800
Huh?

215
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:07,600
Again?

216
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:10,720
I...

217
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:12,320
It's my fault.

218
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:13,400
I'm sorry...

219
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:15,000
The mookrata plan!

220
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:17,560
Look, Plan M works every time.

221
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:19,840
One round of mookrata. Let's go.

222
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:22,840
- Go, go, go. Hurry!
- Mookrata!

223
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:23,840
Come on, Three, Soh.

224
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:27,040
Hey, don't worry.
That was just a warm-up.

225
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,640
Let's go grab some mookrata instead.

226
00:13:29,880 --> 00:13:31,320
Hey, don't worry about it.

227
00:13:31,920 --> 00:13:33,480
Gaming is supposed to be fun.

228
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:35,680
Dive in. Go, go!

229
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:39,320
Hey!

230
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:41,240
- P'Jack...
- Jeez!

231
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:44,200
- Ew.
- You guys are overreacting.

232
00:13:44,280 --> 00:13:45,760
It's just my allergies.

233
00:13:46,040 --> 00:13:47,040
I don't want to take any risks.

234
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:49,000
Here, take this.

235
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,960
- Wow, look at you.
- Hey!

236
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:53,200
If you get sick and miss practice,

237
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:54,760
our team's performance won't just drop.

238
00:13:54,760 --> 00:13:56,320
It'll go straight to hell.

239
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:57,600
For God's sake.

240
00:13:58,560 --> 00:13:59,520
Why so dramatic?

241
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:06,920
Wait, Soh's not here yet?

242
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:08,640
I haven't seen him.

243
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:10,360
He's probably just late.

244
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:12,800
I saw him streaming yesterday
after practice.

245
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:14,280
He wasn't going to quit until he won,

246
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:16,000
but he was on a serious losing streak.

247
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:21,560
He's not home
crying his eyes out right now, is he?

248
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:26,160
Come on.

249
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:29,240
(Hello, P'Three?)

250
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:33,600
Hey, are you crying?

251
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:36,600
- See? Told ya.
- He really is crying.

252
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:48,280
How are you feeling, sick guy?

253
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:49,920
P'Three?

254
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,800
Why did you buy so much stuff?

255
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:55,600
Oh, I just brought you
some healing items.

256
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:10,520
I'm actually feeling better already.

257
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:13,000
You don't have to do all this for me.

258
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:14,840
Oh, come on, kiddo.

259
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:17,920
I just got here,
and you're already kicking me out?

260
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:20,000
Not even a thank-you.

261
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:23,200
I just didn't want to be a bother.

262
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:25,560
Stop talking and just eat.

263
00:15:25,560 --> 00:15:28,200
Here, have some. Eat up...

264
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:30,320
so you can take your meds afterwards.

265
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:40,320
I'll do it myself.

266
00:15:42,880 --> 00:15:45,480
Here, I bought some medicine, too.

267
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:49,640
This one's for your runny nose.
Take it after meals.

268
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:51,240
And...

269
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:55,360
this one's probably for your cough.
Take it before meals.

270
00:15:58,680 --> 00:15:59,560
When should you take this one?

271
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:01,040
After meals.

272
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:02,440
How do you know?

273
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:03,160
Uh...

274
00:16:04,280 --> 00:16:05,800
My mom's a doctor.

275
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:08,080
She stocked up
on plenty of medicine over there.

276
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:19,520
But I've taken most of them,
so they're almost gone.

277
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:22,400
It's actually great
that you bought some to restock for me.

278
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:28,000
You're so kind, P'Three.

279
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:32,680
Well, isn't that obvious?

280
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:35,960
Everyone says I'm a walking red flag,

281
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:39,400
but I'm actually greener
than the Amazon.

282
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:40,360
Not to brag or anything.

283
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:50,800
Here, turn around.

284
00:17:09,080 --> 00:17:10,160
It's secure now.

285
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,160
Here's my first thank-you.

286
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:21,880
Thank you for coming to see me.

287
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:25,960
Otherwise, I would've had to
crawl down to get food myself.

288
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:28,400
Now, my second thank-you.

289
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:31,280
Thank you for buying me all this food.

290
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:33,120
Everything you bought for me...

291
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:34,560
looked so delicious.

292
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:38,040
And this is the third thank-you.

293
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:40,960
Thank you for getting me the medicine.

294
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:45,000
Now I have enough meds
to last me a decade.

295
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:48,000
You'd better give me
a fourth thank-you, too.

296
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:54,080
Because I'm gonna stay
and sponge you down until morning.

297
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:04,120
Here.

298
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,720
Ouch. P'Three, ow!

299
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:10,720
Ow!

300
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:13,600
If you're gonna do it this hard,

301
00:18:14,040 --> 00:18:15,840
give me back my thank-you.

302
00:18:17,440 --> 00:18:20,200
Look at you, whining so much.

303
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:22,480
But when you take heavy damage in-game,

304
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:24,840
I don't hear you complaining one bit.

305
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:27,480
Well, I'm sick right now.

306
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:28,080
What?

307
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:31,800
Didn't you just say you were all better?

308
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:33,320
Were you lying to me?

309
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:35,600
That's not very nice, you know.

310
00:18:36,520 --> 00:18:37,640
Not nice at all.

311
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:45,680
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry.

312
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:46,480
Oh...

313
00:18:48,320 --> 00:18:49,880
Why are you apologizing to me?

314
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:52,640
You're just sponging me down.

315
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:53,960
It's not like I'm bleeding.

316
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:56,560
Then why are you apologizing to me?

317
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:59,000
Do you think
I was scolding you for real?

318
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:00,680
Well...

319
00:19:01,800 --> 00:19:03,720
I haven't been able
to help the team at all,

320
00:19:04,440 --> 00:19:05,480
and I even got sick on top of that.

321
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:08,080
Hey, don't blame yourself like that.

322
00:19:09,680 --> 00:19:11,520
It's actually my fault
for not taking better care of you.

323
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:14,960
Besides, my team
didn't even have things figured out,

324
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:17,880
yet I still went and brought you in.

325
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:25,480
The truth is...

326
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:31,600
I just wanted everyone
to play together and have fun.

327
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:34,160
I'm not even expecting to win anymore.

328
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:36,440
Don't put too much pressure on yourself.

329
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:46,400
(Four, the Favorite Son)

330
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:50,520
(Four, the Favorite Son)

331
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:13,040
Took you long enough to call back, huh?

332
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:14,680
(I'm not in the mood to fight, Four.)

333
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:15,920
Just say what you have to say.

334
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,640
Mom told me to call and ask

335
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:21,720
if you're coming home
for Dad's birthday next week.

336
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:23,520
I'm busy.

337
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:27,680
Seriously, though,

338
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:30,440
are you going to avoid Mom and Dad
for the rest of your life?

339
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:35,800
I'm actually busy.
I have to practice for the Pro League.

340
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,520
At your age...

341
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:41,720
(Do you still think
you can be a champion?)

342
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,200
Hey, age doesn't matter.

343
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:46,240
As long as I can play,
I'm going to keep playing.

344
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:49,040
You, Mom, and Dad
don't have to believe in me.

345
00:20:49,280 --> 00:20:50,600
I'll just win and show you.

346
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:31,080
(Morning, P'Three.)

347
00:21:31,200 --> 00:21:34,960
(I have a morning mission
for you today. Ready, go!)

348
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:37,080
What is he up to now?

349
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:51,040
(New day, HP's still low)

350
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:53,680
(Which item will you choose between...)

351
00:21:58,720 --> 00:22:00,560
(A: If you need caffeine immediately,)

352
00:22:00,600 --> 00:22:02,320
(head to
the resurrection potion extractor.)

353
00:22:02,960 --> 00:22:06,160
(B: If food doesn't matter
and looking good comes first,)

354
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:07,360
(head to the magic mirror.)

355
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:10,280
The resurrection potion extractor?

356
00:22:33,080 --> 00:22:35,520
(This cup restores +50% HP.)

357
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,200
(Next mission...)

358
00:22:50,320 --> 00:22:52,400
(A: Want something to eat?)

359
00:22:52,840 --> 00:22:55,200
(B: Check the news first?)

360
00:22:59,840 --> 00:23:01,720
(My secret recipe
ham and cheese sandwich)

361
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:05,400
(loaded with gooey cheese
restores +100% HP.)

362
00:23:06,920 --> 00:23:07,840
A secret recipe, huh?

363
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:16,640
(HP is full.
Let's do the final mission.)

364
00:23:16,680 --> 00:23:18,560
(Time for the computer.)

365
00:23:20,840 --> 00:23:21,800
Time for the computer?

366
00:23:22,560 --> 00:23:23,200
What now?

367
00:23:32,560 --> 00:23:35,440
(You can use the computer.
I didn't set a password.)

368
00:23:36,200 --> 00:23:37,440
(There's a key in the drawer)

369
00:23:37,760 --> 00:23:39,320
(in case you want to go out.)

370
00:23:48,920 --> 00:23:50,880
(I'm tutoring with James and Arm today.)

371
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:53,160
(Might be back a bit late,
but don't worry.)

372
00:23:53,320 --> 00:23:55,320
(Mr. Bear will be here
to keep you company.)

373
00:23:57,640 --> 00:23:59,880
(Good Morning Thailand by Soh)

374
00:24:02,160 --> 00:24:04,160
(Good Morning Thailand by Soh.)

375
00:24:04,160 --> 00:24:05,400
(Weather Forecast:)

376
00:24:05,440 --> 00:24:06,640
(You're awake.)

377
00:24:06,680 --> 00:24:08,800
(It's a good sign to start a new day.)

378
00:24:08,880 --> 00:24:10,160
(The weather is bright today.)

379
00:24:10,240 --> 00:24:12,000
(Perfect for squeezing in
a practice match.)

380
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:14,320
(Breaking News: One easy target
has been found)

381
00:24:14,360 --> 00:24:16,320
(reading this message.)

382
00:24:20,120 --> 00:24:21,480
(Today's Career Horoscope:)

383
00:24:21,560 --> 00:24:23,640
(It's definitely going to be
a good and smooth day.)

384
00:24:23,680 --> 00:24:25,560
(No matter what you face,
I want you to know...)

385
00:24:25,640 --> 00:24:27,800
(that I'm right here rooting for you.)

386
00:24:27,840 --> 00:24:29,400
(Good luck! From Soh.)

387
00:24:29,520 --> 00:24:30,560
Whoa, Derpy Kid.

388
00:24:38,480 --> 00:24:39,320
Dammit.

389
00:24:39,480 --> 00:24:41,640
Am I smiling right now?

390
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:08,480
You're a mess.

391
00:25:10,520 --> 00:25:12,520
Did you practice so hard
that you got this sick?

392
00:25:13,160 --> 00:25:14,400
Exams are coming up, man.

393
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:18,120
If you can't handle it,
just withdraw.

394
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:21,400
I'm fine. I can handle it.

395
00:25:23,560 --> 00:25:25,920
Don't worry. You're already smart.

396
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:29,800
Arm will tutor you for a bit,
and you'll get it in no time.

397
00:25:35,520 --> 00:25:36,640
Wait, wait.

398
00:25:39,040 --> 00:25:40,760
Am I seeing things?

399
00:25:42,640 --> 00:25:45,160
That's P'Three, right?

400
00:25:50,840 --> 00:25:52,200
What is he doing here?

401
00:25:59,920 --> 00:26:01,920
Did you come to see me
for something urgent?

402
00:26:03,240 --> 00:26:04,000
Oh...

403
00:26:04,720 --> 00:26:06,800
Oh, well, I came...

404
00:26:07,360 --> 00:26:10,080
to ask you to pick out a gift with me
for P'Toobtub's baby.

405
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:12,840
Wanna come along?

406
00:26:14,760 --> 00:26:15,520
I do.

407
00:26:16,400 --> 00:26:17,640
I just finished tutoring.

408
00:26:18,200 --> 00:26:19,000
Let's go, shall we?

409
00:26:20,800 --> 00:26:21,520
Sure.

410
00:26:32,440 --> 00:26:34,120
You don't have to carry my bag for me.

411
00:26:35,440 --> 00:26:36,880
I can carry it myself.

412
00:26:38,560 --> 00:26:39,720
Uh, well, I...

413
00:26:42,240 --> 00:26:43,360
No... Never mind.

414
00:26:44,080 --> 00:26:45,920
Shall we go buy it now?

415
00:26:46,240 --> 00:26:47,760
Or we'll be late for the training camp.

416
00:26:48,320 --> 00:26:49,080
Okay.

417
00:27:00,560 --> 00:27:02,040
You're thinking
what I'm thinking, right?

418
00:27:02,520 --> 00:27:04,040
Don't you think it's a bit weird?

419
00:27:04,560 --> 00:27:05,440
Are you thinking the same thing?

420
00:27:06,920 --> 00:27:07,840
What are you thinking?

421
00:27:10,600 --> 00:27:11,880
Something's definitely off.

422
00:27:13,080 --> 00:27:13,680
Oh...

423
00:27:24,800 --> 00:27:26,200
Hey, thanks.

424
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:29,400
Hey, *sshole! That's mine.

425
00:27:29,720 --> 00:27:31,800
- Why are you drinking that?
- Can't I have a sip?

426
00:27:32,280 --> 00:27:34,680
- You have your own.
- But I wanted green tea.

427
00:27:38,080 --> 00:27:40,320
(Coaching Conversation)

428
00:27:52,360 --> 00:27:53,960
(Parenting)

429
00:28:00,400 --> 00:28:01,600
You're really serious, aren't you?

430
00:28:03,080 --> 00:28:04,600
It's just a gift for the baby.

431
00:28:06,120 --> 00:28:07,480
Well, I'm just excited.

432
00:28:08,760 --> 00:28:11,200
I can't wait to read bedtime stories
to the baby.

433
00:28:12,160 --> 00:28:13,080
I'm confused.

434
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:15,200
Why are you so hyped up?

435
00:28:15,880 --> 00:28:18,280
It's because I'm an only child.

436
00:28:19,120 --> 00:28:21,880
Whenever it's about kids, I...

437
00:28:23,040 --> 00:28:24,280
get really invested.

438
00:28:26,440 --> 00:28:27,440
It's kind of strange, isn't it?

439
00:28:28,200 --> 00:28:30,480
An only child wants siblings,

440
00:28:30,800 --> 00:28:32,080
while those with siblings...

441
00:28:32,240 --> 00:28:33,680
wish they were an only child.

442
00:28:35,080 --> 00:28:37,280
I think you're lucky, though.

443
00:28:38,080 --> 00:28:40,560
It's like having a best friend
who's grown up with you since day one.

444
00:28:40,680 --> 00:28:44,320
You might fight or argue sometimes,

445
00:28:45,320 --> 00:28:47,920
but you're still on the same team.

446
00:28:49,880 --> 00:28:50,600
Wait,

447
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:54,200
were you eavesdropping on my call?

448
00:29:02,040 --> 00:29:04,040
But I didn't want to fight anymore,

449
00:29:04,480 --> 00:29:07,560
so I moved out to live on my own,

450
00:29:07,960 --> 00:29:10,200
doing things my parents think
are a waste of time.

451
00:29:10,800 --> 00:29:14,760
And my younger brother
probably thinks I'm a loser.

452
00:29:17,880 --> 00:29:20,200
But I've made up my mind
that I won't go back.

453
00:29:22,120 --> 00:29:24,040
Not until I can buy a house,

454
00:29:24,920 --> 00:29:25,840
get a car,

455
00:29:26,440 --> 00:29:27,880
and have millions in savings.

456
00:29:29,360 --> 00:29:31,520
Then I'll go show off
right in front of my parents,

457
00:29:32,240 --> 00:29:33,760
so they'll finally stop
looking down on me.

458
00:29:35,960 --> 00:29:39,000
Don't you ever get homesick, though?

459
00:29:45,280 --> 00:29:46,400
Of course I do.

460
00:29:50,360 --> 00:29:52,080
Don't you try
to talk me into going back.

461
00:29:53,560 --> 00:29:54,920
I've already decided.

462
00:29:59,360 --> 00:30:00,920
That's not what I meant.

463
00:30:02,760 --> 00:30:03,600
I understand

464
00:30:03,720 --> 00:30:06,720
that your goals are important, too.

465
00:30:22,280 --> 00:30:25,240
But even if you don't go yourself,

466
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:27,240
you can still send a gift, right?

467
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:44,440
Will it really work, Derpy Kid?

468
00:30:44,760 --> 00:30:46,440
My family owns a gold store.

469
00:30:46,640 --> 00:30:47,640
They're way richer than me.

470
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:49,720
They wouldn't care
about shoes like these.

471
00:30:50,280 --> 00:30:52,120
If it were an expensive watch,
that'd be a different story.

472
00:30:53,280 --> 00:30:55,400
The best things
don't have to be expensive.

473
00:31:07,760 --> 00:31:08,920
Whoa, whoa. Hey.

474
00:31:09,320 --> 00:31:10,000
You don't have to.

475
00:31:22,160 --> 00:31:22,640
So,

476
00:31:23,800 --> 00:31:25,800
is this how Cinderella feels?

477
00:31:27,280 --> 00:31:28,480
All done, P'Three.

478
00:31:29,480 --> 00:31:31,520
Stand up and try walking in them.

479
00:31:36,640 --> 00:31:37,280
Whoa.

480
00:31:39,120 --> 00:31:40,560
These are so comfortable.

481
00:31:41,040 --> 00:31:43,880
Is this how the heroes feel
when they get god-tier boots?

482
00:31:44,560 --> 00:31:45,840
Of course, P'Three.

483
00:31:46,240 --> 00:31:47,720
When you wear good shoes,

484
00:31:47,760 --> 00:31:49,240
it prevents your feet from aching.

485
00:31:49,640 --> 00:31:51,240
And when you walk a lot,

486
00:31:51,280 --> 00:31:52,880
it prevents back pain, too.

487
00:31:54,040 --> 00:31:55,960
That's why I buy them
for my mom all the time.

488
00:31:58,280 --> 00:31:59,400
Good health...

489
00:31:59,880 --> 00:32:01,560
is something no amount of money can buy.

490
00:32:19,040 --> 00:32:21,080
I hope my parents and Four
will like them.

491
00:32:25,360 --> 00:32:27,520
(We are B.S. Brothers)

492
00:32:27,560 --> 00:32:28,320
Here it is.

493
00:32:28,760 --> 00:32:30,160
Thanks a lot, Soh.

494
00:32:30,280 --> 00:32:32,240
The baby is still
just an embryo, though.

495
00:32:32,240 --> 00:32:33,280
Why are you in such a rush
to buy things?

496
00:32:33,800 --> 00:32:34,320
Wait.

497
00:32:34,480 --> 00:32:37,360
P'Three said you wanted a gift
for the baby already.

498
00:32:39,440 --> 00:32:40,200
Hold on a second.

499
00:32:41,600 --> 00:32:43,920
So P'Three...

500
00:32:44,600 --> 00:32:48,520
told Soh he wanted
to buy something for P'Toobtub?

501
00:32:48,760 --> 00:32:51,720
And the two of you
went shopping alone together?

502
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:52,640
Huh?

503
00:32:52,920 --> 00:32:54,000
Well...

504
00:32:54,320 --> 00:32:56,920
I've heard P'Toobtub
complaining quite a lot

505
00:32:56,920 --> 00:32:58,680
about needing to put all his money
back into the shop.

506
00:32:58,680 --> 00:33:01,200
And with the baby coming soon,

507
00:33:01,200 --> 00:33:02,960
he'd have to buy baby stuff, too.

508
00:33:03,640 --> 00:33:07,440
So we just wanted to help
lighten the load.

509
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:10,400
Wait, Three, when did I
ever complain to you?

510
00:33:10,440 --> 00:33:11,240
You did say it!

511
00:33:12,480 --> 00:33:15,600
Oh, right, yeah.
I guess I did say that.

512
00:33:16,280 --> 00:33:19,360
I really wanted it, right?
The one I sent you in the chat.

513
00:33:19,400 --> 00:33:21,240
- That's great.
- Yeah, bro.

514
00:33:21,280 --> 00:33:23,520
- Thanks a lot, my dear bros.
- Don't mention it.

515
00:33:25,480 --> 00:33:27,680
Anyway, are you all better now, Soh?

516
00:33:27,840 --> 00:33:29,440
Yes, I'm all better.

517
00:33:32,280 --> 00:33:33,520
I'm sorry to everyone

518
00:33:33,560 --> 00:33:35,360
for missing practice for so many days.

519
00:33:35,720 --> 00:33:36,640
But I promise

520
00:33:36,680 --> 00:33:39,600
that I'll hurry
and catch up with all of you.

521
00:33:40,880 --> 00:33:42,120
I definitely won't drag the team down.

522
00:33:43,400 --> 00:33:44,320
It's fine.

523
00:33:44,480 --> 00:33:46,480
No need to be so serious
about stuff like this.

524
00:33:46,840 --> 00:33:48,520
Our team is cursed anyway.

525
00:33:48,560 --> 00:33:49,720
No matter how we play,

526
00:33:49,760 --> 00:33:51,560
we never make it to the finals.

527
00:33:51,920 --> 00:33:54,440
I'm not surprised
P'Pech wants to disband the team.

528
00:33:55,840 --> 00:33:56,800
What?

529
00:33:56,960 --> 00:33:58,240
That's some bad luck talk right there.

530
00:34:00,480 --> 00:34:04,760
What Laem said might sound harsh,

531
00:34:06,080 --> 00:34:08,680
but I've prepared myself
for the worst, too.

532
00:34:13,560 --> 00:34:16,360
It's true that
our team had its glory days,

533
00:34:17,280 --> 00:34:19,160
but look at how old we are now.

534
00:34:19,600 --> 00:34:22,200
Who knows if we can even keep up
with the younger players.

535
00:34:24,480 --> 00:34:27,440
I think this tournament

536
00:34:27,560 --> 00:34:29,840
might be the last one for us.

537
00:34:30,720 --> 00:34:31,520
Come on.

538
00:34:32,120 --> 00:34:33,120
What's up with that?

539
00:34:33,600 --> 00:34:35,760
I was in such a good mood today.

540
00:34:36,240 --> 00:34:37,600
You just made me so depressed.

541
00:34:39,560 --> 00:34:41,680
If this is going to be
our last tournament,

542
00:34:42,520 --> 00:34:44,360
shall we give it everything we've got?

543
00:34:52,400 --> 00:34:53,080
Hey,

544
00:34:53,240 --> 00:34:55,520
how long has it been
since we were at the top?

545
00:34:57,080 --> 00:34:58,600
I miss the view from up there.

546
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:02,600
Shall we try one more time

547
00:35:02,640 --> 00:35:03,800
to go breathe that summit air?

548
00:35:03,880 --> 00:35:05,960
Yeah, that's the spirit,

549
00:35:06,040 --> 00:35:07,400
Son of Wanphen!

550
00:35:07,440 --> 00:35:08,760
Dude, I don't mind you

551
00:35:08,760 --> 00:35:09,720
making fun of my mom's name.

552
00:35:09,760 --> 00:35:12,160
But if you don't play like a beast
on match day,

553
00:35:12,160 --> 00:35:13,240
I'm definitely smacking your head.

554
00:35:13,280 --> 00:35:15,480
- Bring it on!
- Just you wait. I'll...

555
00:35:16,480 --> 00:35:17,360
Stop!

556
00:35:17,400 --> 00:35:18,680
Let's do a team huddle.

557
00:35:26,360 --> 00:35:30,680
- Talk your sh*t, take the championship!
- Talk your sh*t, take the championship!

558
00:35:33,600 --> 00:35:35,320
I really want to breathe
that air up top.

559
00:35:36,040 --> 00:35:37,760
- Wow, so refreshing.
- How is it?

560
00:35:37,800 --> 00:35:39,080
Refreshing, man. So refreshing.

561
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:43,840
We've gotta get back up there
to breathe that air.

562
00:35:43,880 --> 00:35:44,760
Exactly.

563
00:35:47,880 --> 00:35:49,760
Oh, you're back, son?

564
00:35:49,840 --> 00:35:51,040
You're back so late today.

565
00:35:51,960 --> 00:35:53,320
Have you eaten anything yet?

566
00:35:53,560 --> 00:35:54,680
Yes, Mom.

567
00:35:56,200 --> 00:35:57,000
Look at this.

568
00:35:59,280 --> 00:36:02,360
Today, I was going through
some old things

569
00:36:02,760 --> 00:36:04,600
as I was planning to
sell them by weight,

570
00:36:05,360 --> 00:36:09,040
and I found
your high school friendship journal.

571
00:36:17,880 --> 00:36:20,440
Right, how is Ten doing?

572
00:36:22,160 --> 00:36:23,560
Ever since you graduated from college,

573
00:36:23,880 --> 00:36:25,960
I haven't seen him
come visit our house at all.

574
00:36:27,760 --> 00:36:29,320
He's just busy with work, Mom.

575
00:36:30,080 --> 00:36:31,320
I've been pretty busy myself.

576
00:36:31,800 --> 00:36:32,960
We haven't talked much.

577
00:36:34,880 --> 00:36:37,320
So, I'm going up to take a shower now.

578
00:36:54,880 --> 00:36:56,720
(To Jack, my lovely friend.
Hi, Jack, I'm Noey from Class 6/3.)

579
00:36:56,760 --> 00:36:57,720
(Congrats on getting into college.
Hope to see you again.)

580
00:36:57,760 --> 00:36:59,600
(Wishing you happiness and good friends.
I'm glad we're friends.)

581
00:37:02,720 --> 00:37:03,920
(To Jack, my best friend. From Ten,
the friend who loves you the most.)

582
00:37:03,960 --> 00:37:04,760
(I hope you live a happy life)

583
00:37:04,760 --> 00:37:06,080
(and get to do everything you want.
I'm so glad I met you.)

584
00:37:25,440 --> 00:37:26,400
(Wanna play ranked?)

585
00:37:54,440 --> 00:37:56,000
(Thanks for carrying me again.)

586
00:37:56,240 --> 00:37:57,840
(If you hadn't healed me
in that last second,)

587
00:37:57,920 --> 00:37:58,840
(I'd definitely be dead.)

588
00:38:04,080 --> 00:38:06,000
(I'm used to carrying you by now.)

589
00:38:09,120 --> 00:38:10,520
(Going to sleep now.)

590
00:38:13,960 --> 00:38:17,360
(Oh, and I'm pretty busy lately.)

591
00:38:17,720 --> 00:38:19,760
(I might not be able to
play ranked with you much.)

592
00:38:23,080 --> 00:38:24,760
(Are you training
for the Pro League or something?)

593
00:38:25,040 --> 00:38:27,600
(Probably not. You play like trash.)

594
00:38:33,240 --> 00:38:34,120
(You never know.)

595
00:38:34,520 --> 00:38:36,960
(You might be carrying
an esports pro right now.)

596
00:38:38,920 --> 00:38:40,160
(Why are you being so mysterious?)

597
00:38:40,160 --> 00:38:40,920
(I'm getting scared.)

598
00:38:41,120 --> 00:38:43,240
(Who am I actually friends with here?)

599
00:38:48,880 --> 00:38:51,760
Let's meet up when we're free.

600
00:39:15,960 --> 00:39:17,640
I want to meet you in person, too.

601
00:39:25,360 --> 00:39:27,200
P'Pech gave us the orders.

602
00:39:28,600 --> 00:39:29,560
We've gotta...

603
00:39:29,920 --> 00:39:32,160
win the first match to set the tone

604
00:39:32,800 --> 00:39:34,840
and gain momentum to get the advantage.

605
00:39:34,960 --> 00:39:36,360
Yes, let's do this!

606
00:39:36,560 --> 00:39:37,520
- Let's go.
- Come on.

607
00:39:37,600 --> 00:39:38,840
- Let's do it.
- Let's do it.

608
00:39:39,760 --> 00:39:41,440
But you're facing Kingdom
in the first match.

609
00:39:41,480 --> 00:39:42,920
- Oh, come on!
- What?

610
00:39:43,480 --> 00:39:44,840
What the hell?

611
00:39:45,520 --> 00:39:46,800
I'm not playing.

612
00:39:46,960 --> 00:39:48,040
Change the game.

613
00:39:48,280 --> 00:39:49,200
Calm down.

614
00:39:49,560 --> 00:39:51,280
If you can beat the first team,

615
00:39:51,600 --> 00:39:52,680
it'll be a great start.

616
00:39:53,720 --> 00:39:55,000
But even if you don't win,

617
00:39:55,040 --> 00:39:56,800
you still have a chance
to redeem yourselves.

618
00:39:57,960 --> 00:39:59,200
Don't stress about it.

619
00:40:00,080 --> 00:40:01,120
If you're under too much pressure,

620
00:40:01,160 --> 00:40:03,640
the team might lose their nerve,
and it won't be good.

621
00:40:04,040 --> 00:40:05,960
Just play according to your usual form,

622
00:40:06,080 --> 00:40:07,800
but you have to stay focused.

623
00:40:08,200 --> 00:40:09,520
Focus. Keep that in mind.

624
00:40:11,200 --> 00:40:14,920
I'm already shook
just hearing the team's name.

625
00:40:15,520 --> 00:40:16,760
We're doomed.

626
00:40:18,280 --> 00:40:19,440
It's a total nightmare.

627
00:40:19,880 --> 00:40:24,080
We've played 14 matches
and lost all 14 of them.

628
00:40:25,320 --> 00:40:27,520
It's like they've got us
all figured out.

629
00:40:34,160 --> 00:40:34,920
Hey,

630
00:40:35,480 --> 00:40:37,080
but this time,
things are gonna be different

631
00:40:37,240 --> 00:40:39,160
because we've got a joker up our sleeve.

632
00:40:40,320 --> 00:40:41,920
They'll never see us coming.

633
00:40:46,200 --> 00:40:46,920
Me?

634
00:40:47,320 --> 00:40:47,880
Yeah.

635
00:40:49,080 --> 00:40:50,320
The secret weapon.

636
00:40:54,960 --> 00:40:56,120
What a huge surprise!

637
00:40:56,160 --> 00:40:58,640
Here's B.S. Brothers' lineup
for this season,

638
00:40:58,680 --> 00:41:02,600
featuring their brand-new Support,
Derya MK12!

639
00:41:02,640 --> 00:41:03,720
Whoa, that name?

640
00:41:03,760 --> 00:41:07,080
I bet the shippers
are screaming right now.

641
00:41:07,120 --> 00:41:08,480
They're going to be losing it

642
00:41:08,520 --> 00:41:12,080
as the fan-favorite ship, Three and Soh,
is finally on display.

643
00:41:12,080 --> 00:41:13,680
Wow, they're really well-known.

644
00:41:13,840 --> 00:41:14,640
We'll have to see

645
00:41:14,640 --> 00:41:18,240
just how much of a change
Derya will bring to the team,

646
00:41:18,400 --> 00:41:21,160
especially in this first match
where they face Kingdom,

647
00:41:21,280 --> 00:41:23,880
one of the top-tier teams
from last year, man.

648
00:41:23,920 --> 00:41:25,360
Will they be able to handle it, P'Win?

649
00:41:25,440 --> 00:41:27,360
Looking at the buzz in our community,

650
00:41:27,360 --> 00:41:28,960
(3-0 for sure, no doubt)
it's looking like a total sweep.

651
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:29,960
(Losers are just losers)
It's a sweep.

652
00:41:29,960 --> 00:41:31,880
(Derya who? Never heard of him)
It's definitely gonna be 3-0.

653
00:41:31,880 --> 00:41:33,880
Now the question is can B.S. Brothers

654
00:41:33,880 --> 00:41:34,760
prove the doubters wrong?

655
00:41:34,760 --> 00:41:35,840
We'll just have to wait and see.

656
00:41:37,640 --> 00:41:40,120
Today's the day everyone finds out

657
00:41:40,200 --> 00:41:42,400
that B.S. Brothers
is more than just talk.

658
00:41:48,120 --> 00:41:49,960
(See you at the studio
after the exam.)

659
00:41:50,840 --> 00:41:51,640
(No rush.)

660
00:41:51,840 --> 00:41:53,920
(We've got plenty of time
to put on a show for them today.)

661
00:42:33,760 --> 00:42:34,520
(Listen up, everyone.)

662
00:42:34,600 --> 00:42:37,400
(The 14-0 record of B.S. Brothers)

663
00:42:37,440 --> 00:42:38,920
(is definitely going to happen again)

664
00:42:38,960 --> 00:42:40,120
(because they're unlucky enough)

665
00:42:40,160 --> 00:42:42,360
(to run into Kingdom
in the first match.)

666
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:44,160
Oh, but right now,

667
00:42:44,200 --> 00:42:46,680
there's a bit of buzz going around,
whispering that

668
00:42:46,880 --> 00:42:49,960
a new member named Derya MK12

669
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:53,280
might turn things around,
but who knows if he actually can.

670
00:42:53,360 --> 00:42:54,800
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

671
00:42:54,960 --> 00:42:56,320
Hold on a second, bro.

672
00:42:56,360 --> 00:42:57,440
We've got an insider.

673
00:42:57,640 --> 00:43:00,680
(Someone sent me a video
of B.S. Brothers practicing.)

674
00:43:00,960 --> 00:43:02,720
(Let's take a look at it first.)

675
00:43:03,680 --> 00:43:06,480
- (Mid skills, just clout chasers.)
- Jeez, kid.

676
00:43:06,560 --> 00:43:07,680
What kind of play is that?

677
00:43:07,720 --> 00:43:09,640
(He's got nothing special.)
You're better off staying home.

678
00:43:09,640 --> 00:43:13,200
(Without Three, nobody would've cared.)
Don't think B.S. Brothers will make it.

679
00:43:16,520 --> 00:43:18,000
(He's even afraid
to take off his head mask.)

680
00:43:18,040 --> 00:43:20,200
(Scared of being embarrassed
when you lose, huh? LOL)

681
00:43:20,680 --> 00:43:21,440
(Donating a hundred.)

682
00:43:21,480 --> 00:43:23,720
(Need some friends to jump him
and rip that bear head off.)

683
00:43:23,760 --> 00:43:26,040
(I hate those who try too hard
to have a gimmick.)

684
00:43:28,520 --> 00:43:29,760
(The team would be better off
without him.)

685
00:43:29,760 --> 00:43:32,120
(Want to bet that Derya
will definitely cost them the game?)

686
00:43:35,840 --> 00:43:38,040
(D-Day)

687
00:43:38,960 --> 00:43:40,800
Sh*t, this is bad.

688
00:43:41,280 --> 00:43:42,400
Guys, check this out.

689
00:43:45,480 --> 00:43:48,480
- (Such a noob.)
- Sh*t.

690
00:43:49,080 --> 00:43:50,760
The haters are swarming in.

691
00:43:51,280 --> 00:43:53,040
Soh is getting trashed.

692
00:43:53,720 --> 00:43:54,880
What should we do?

693
00:43:55,440 --> 00:43:57,760
If Soh sees this,
he won't be able to handle it.

694
00:43:58,160 --> 00:43:59,840
I bet he's already seen it.

695
00:43:59,880 --> 00:44:01,160
The video just blew up.

696
00:44:02,200 --> 00:44:04,200
He's still not here,
and the match is about to begin.

697
00:44:07,400 --> 00:44:09,440
B.S. Brothers, please stand by.

698
00:44:09,880 --> 00:44:11,160
Give us a second, please.

699
00:44:13,640 --> 00:44:14,720
How's it going, Three?

700
00:44:14,880 --> 00:44:15,920
The match is starting, man.

701
00:44:18,000 --> 00:44:20,840
Hey, Nuii, Pod, settle it with
a game of rock, paper, scissors.

702
00:44:20,920 --> 00:44:22,480
Winner subs in for Soh.

703
00:44:22,520 --> 00:44:23,080
Yeah.

704
00:44:23,440 --> 00:44:24,320
Do it.

705
00:44:24,640 --> 00:44:26,120
Yeah, go.

706
00:44:30,120 --> 00:44:30,640
Here we go.

707
00:44:31,480 --> 00:44:32,880
Today's my day to shine.

708
00:44:33,480 --> 00:44:36,280
Guys, give it your all. We have to win.

709
00:44:43,840 --> 00:44:46,360
Come on, come on. First game, let's go.

710
00:44:48,960 --> 00:44:50,680
(All Creeps Deployed)

711
00:44:51,400 --> 00:44:53,600
- Let's trail them first.
- Got it.

712
00:45:02,520 --> 00:45:03,360
Wait...

713
00:45:03,720 --> 00:45:04,960
What the hell was that?

714
00:45:05,440 --> 00:45:06,800
Isn't that a bit too fast?

715
00:45:07,400 --> 00:45:08,240
Sorry.

716
00:45:08,400 --> 00:45:10,040
- Try again. Focus!
- Okay.

717
00:45:10,080 --> 00:45:11,360
Hey, the Support isn't that good.

718
00:45:11,360 --> 00:45:13,680
- Looking good. This is easy.
- Wow, just one minute in.

719
00:45:13,680 --> 00:45:15,440
and we've already got First Blood.
Nuii just got taken out.

720
00:45:15,480 --> 00:45:17,360
He mispositioned himself,
and it showed.

721
00:45:17,400 --> 00:45:19,480
Wow, they're being chased down hard.

722
00:45:19,480 --> 00:45:21,040
Pod and Nuii are under heavy pressure.

723
00:45:21,080 --> 00:45:23,240
They're literally running
behind the tower.

724
00:45:23,280 --> 00:45:26,000
This looks like an early game disaster.

725
00:45:26,040 --> 00:45:26,960
They probably won't make it.

726
00:45:28,240 --> 00:45:30,840
Sh*t, where the hell is Soh?

727
00:45:31,840 --> 00:45:33,400
Maybe he couldn't take it

728
00:45:33,600 --> 00:45:34,920
and withdrew before the match?

729
00:45:36,760 --> 00:45:37,640
Then what are we gonna do?

730
00:45:38,440 --> 00:45:39,520
How would I know?

731
00:46:05,720 --> 00:46:06,480
P'Three?

732
00:46:08,160 --> 00:46:09,240
Are you doing okay, kiddo?

733
00:46:20,720 --> 00:46:21,960
What are you doing here?

734
00:46:22,680 --> 00:46:24,160
What about the match?

735
00:46:27,120 --> 00:46:29,800
Well, I saw your HP dropping,

736
00:46:30,080 --> 00:46:31,360
so I teleported here to heal you.

737
00:46:42,360 --> 00:46:44,080
Is this your first time getting trashed?

738
00:46:44,200 --> 00:46:45,200
Freaked out, didn't you?

739
00:46:47,400 --> 00:46:48,000
Yeah.

740
00:46:48,760 --> 00:46:50,720
But I understand.

741
00:46:52,400 --> 00:46:53,640
My dad once told me that...

742
00:46:55,600 --> 00:46:56,760
people who aren't hated

743
00:46:57,680 --> 00:46:59,240
are the ones who are invisible.

744
00:47:01,280 --> 00:47:02,320
I'm not invisible.

745
00:47:03,200 --> 00:47:04,680
That's why I get hated on.

746
00:47:06,840 --> 00:47:07,800
I get it.

747
00:47:07,960 --> 00:47:09,240
I've dealt with it my whole life, too.

748
00:47:10,400 --> 00:47:13,520
I even wondered,
"What the hell did I ever do to them?"

749
00:47:14,280 --> 00:47:16,360
But as I got older, I realized

750
00:47:17,200 --> 00:47:19,160
you can't make everyone like you.

751
00:47:20,400 --> 00:47:22,920
And to be fair,
I can be kind of an *sshole sometimes.

752
00:47:27,760 --> 00:47:29,000
All I can do now

753
00:47:29,920 --> 00:47:31,720
is choose what to focus on.

754
00:47:32,520 --> 00:47:33,920
It's the same for you, Derpy Kid.

755
00:47:35,080 --> 00:47:38,040
Just focus on the people
who actually care about you.

756
00:47:42,200 --> 00:47:43,720
The people who care about me?

757
00:47:46,640 --> 00:47:47,960
You don't have to look very far.

758
00:47:48,080 --> 00:47:48,960
I'm right here.

759
00:47:52,720 --> 00:47:54,240
I mean...

760
00:47:55,000 --> 00:47:57,000
Me and the B.S. Brothers members.

761
00:48:02,560 --> 00:48:04,640
As for those who don't like us,

762
00:48:05,120 --> 00:48:07,560
there's nothing we can do
to change their minds.

763
00:48:09,120 --> 00:48:10,160
But think about it.

764
00:48:11,440 --> 00:48:13,760
If their lives were actually going well,

765
00:48:14,480 --> 00:48:16,560
why would they spend their time
trashing us

766
00:48:17,600 --> 00:48:19,280
just to make themselves feel better?

767
00:48:28,080 --> 00:48:30,280
Whatever your reason was
for coming here,

768
00:48:32,280 --> 00:48:33,280
thank you.

769
00:48:36,120 --> 00:48:36,920
And...

770
00:48:38,520 --> 00:48:39,520
I'm sorry

771
00:48:40,480 --> 00:48:42,160
for causing such a mess.

772
00:48:43,920 --> 00:48:46,160
I shouldn't have put you
through all this trouble.

773
00:48:58,640 --> 00:49:01,760
(Today's mission is
to choose what your heart desires.)

774
00:49:01,760 --> 00:49:05,480
(A: Recall. Open the door
and we'll fight this out together.)

775
00:49:05,560 --> 00:49:09,640
(B: Surrender. Just tell me.
I'll understand and walk away.)

776
00:49:09,760 --> 00:49:13,160
(P.S. Either way,
I'm always by your side.)

777
00:49:18,960 --> 00:49:20,080
I came here

778
00:49:20,560 --> 00:49:22,440
just to make sure you're still okay.

779
00:49:23,760 --> 00:49:26,360
If you can't handle it,
or if you're not ready to go back,

780
00:49:26,400 --> 00:49:27,920
it's totally fine. I understand.

781
00:49:29,720 --> 00:49:33,000
Right now, your feelings
are what matter most.

782
00:49:34,760 --> 00:49:35,800
You got that, kiddo?

783
00:50:02,240 --> 00:50:03,960
So, you okay?

784
00:50:10,880 --> 00:50:13,720
(The Blue Team's tower
has been destroyed)

785
00:50:14,200 --> 00:50:15,200
We can end it.

786
00:50:15,240 --> 00:50:16,720
- Hurry, hurry!
